                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "071ef6a9-2348-3bfb-a5ef-23b6a8d27b6d",
                        "entry_id": "15b06977-1a5c-35fe-b5d1-3aaab60dd645",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prudential plc, a financial services company based in the United Kingdom."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20dcdd74-46e1-4b4d-9b1b-d147ae5fafe5",
                                "sense_id": "071ef6a9-2348-3bfb-a5ef-23b6a8d27b6d",
                                "text": "So, against its original aims in buying the firm — but convinced by Mr Ball that this was the direction in which to go — the Pru followed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "171723c0-5d0a-4b59-b9be-9f9678a3d2eb",
                                "sense_id": "071ef6a9-2348-3bfb-a5ef-23b6a8d27b6d",
                                "text": "Also during the 1990s, the Pru aggressively jumped into the group insurance business, the purchase by companies of insurance policies for groups of workers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be8a4753-6e2f-4221-9bcc-3075ecc83619",
                                "sense_id": "071ef6a9-2348-3bfb-a5ef-23b6a8d27b6d",
                                "text": "In B2B situations where The Pru and Equitable Life jointly provide products, the business has tended to shift towards The Pru."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
